#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# toeplitz_matrix

#% text
# `toeplitz_matrix(c)` gives the Hermitian Toeplitz matrix with first column `c`; `toeplitz_matrix(c, r)` has first row `r`; `toeplitz_matrix(n)` has entries |i - j| + 1.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The entry in row `i` and column `j` depends only on `i - j`.

#% item
# With one list the first row is the complex conjugate of the first column, so the matrix is Hermitian.

#% item
# The matrix is `length(c)` by `length(r)`; the first entry of `r` is ignored.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
toeplitz_matrix(4)
#% output
#= [[1, 2, 3, 4], [2, 1, 2, 3], [3, 2, 1, 2], [4, 3, 2, 1]]

#% cell
toeplitz_matrix([a, b, c, d])
#% output
#= [[a, b, c, d], [b, a, b, c], [c, b, a, b], [d, c, b, a]]

#% cell
toeplitz_matrix([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [1, 6, 7])
#% output
#= [[1, 6, 7], [2, 1, 6], [3, 2, 1], [4, 3, 2], [5, 4, 3]]

#% cell
toeplitz_matrix([1 + 2*im, 3 + 4*im, 5 + 6*im])
#% output
#= [[1 + 2im, 3 - 4im, 5 - 6im], [3 + 4im, 1 + 2im, 3 - 4im], [5 + 6im, 3 + 4im, 1 + 2im]]

#% cell
toeplitz_matrix([1., 2., 4., 8.], [1., 0.5, 0.25, 0.125])
#% output
#= [[1.0, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125], [2.0, 1.0, 0.5, 0.25], [4.0, 2.0, 1.0, 0.5], [8.0, 4.0, 2.0, 1.0]]

